Task 1: Install and Run sosreport
Subtask 1.1: Install sosreport
sudo dnf install sos -y
Expected Outcome:
Package sos is installed with no errors.

Troubleshooting:
If encountering dependency issues:

sudo dnf clean all
sudo dnf makecache
Subtask 1.2: Generate Diagnostic Report
sudo sosreport --batch --name=$(hostname)
Key Concepts:

--batch: Runs non-interactively
--name: Tags the report with the hostname
Expected Outcome:
A .tar.xz file is created in /var/tmp/ with system diagnostics.

Note:
The exact filename will be shown in the command output.

Task 2: Install and Register insights-client
Subtask 2.1: Install the Client
sudo dnf install insights-client -y
Subtask 2.2: Register the System
sudo insights-client --register
Expected Outcome:
"Successfully registered host to Red Hat Insights" message.

Troubleshooting:
If registration fails:

Verify subscription status:
sudo subscription-manager status
Check network access to cloud.redhat.com
Subtask 2.3: Perform First Upload
sudo insights-client
Key Concepts:
This uploads system data to the Insights portal for analysis.

Task 3: Analyze Reports via Red Hat Insights Portal
Subtask 3.1: Access the Portal
Navigate to: https://cloud.redhat.com/insights
Log in with your Red Hat account
Subtask 3.2: Review System Insights
Locate your system under "Systems" tab
Examine:
Advisories: Recommended updates
Subscriptions: Compliance status
Performance: Resource utilization trends
Key Features:

Risk identification
Proactive issue detection
Remediation guidance
